@startuml end-to-end
title OIIE end to end — current state\nAuthoring → dispatch → governance → consumption → inspection

skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign left
skinparam maxMessageSize 240
skinparam ParticipantPadding 12
skinparam BoxPadding 12

actor "Engineer" as EngUser
actor "Location steward" as StewardUser
actor "Maintenance planner" as PlannerUser
actor "Demonstrator" as Demo

box "SimHost — simulated participants"
  participant "ENG" as ENG
  participant "REG-LOCATION" as LOC
  participant "MMS" as MMS
end box

box "SimHost — run visualisation"
  participant "Blazor UI" as UI
end box

participant "ws-ISBM provider" as ISBM
participant "ws-CIR provider" as CIR

== 0. Reset ==

Demo -> UI : Reset  /  Day zero
activate UI
UI -> ISBM : close sessions, purge sandbox channels
note right of UI
  /OIIE/CIR/Request is **never** deleted. It belongs
  to the CIR provider and holds its long-lived
  provider-request session; deleting it would break
  the provider for every participant.
end note
UI -> ENG : truncate + reload class fixtures
UI -> LOC : truncate + reload class fixtures
UI -> MMS : truncate — **no fixtures to load**
UI --> Demo : counts per participant\nENG 4 classes / REG-LOCATION 2 / MMS 0
deactivate UI

note over ENG, MMS
  The asymmetry is the product, not an oversight.
  Equal counts here would mean a fixture leaked and
  the demonstration is no longer showing anything.
end note

== 1. Authoring ==

EngUser -> ENG : edit tags in Unit 101
activate ENG
ENG -> ENG : classify against\nrdl:TemperatureIndicatingController
ENG -> ENG : persist Tag rows + property values\n(Control action = Reverse)
ENG --> EngUser : work in progress
deactivate ENG

EngUser -> ENG : promote named version "Rev C"
activate ENG
ENG -> ENG : validation gate against\nthe effective property set
alt findings present
  ENG --> EngUser : promotion blocked\nValidationFinding list
else gate passes
  ENG -> ENG : commit NamedVersion + Outbox rows\n(single transaction)
  note right of ENG
    The BOD is derived from committed rows.
    A form never authors a BOD directly.
  end note
end
deactivate ENG

== 2. Registration and dispatch ==

ENG -> ISBM : PostRequest(ProcessRegistry)
activate ISBM
ISBM -> CIR : deliver
activate CIR
CIR -> CIR : SourceID=ENG, assign CIRIDs
CIR -> ISBM : AcknowledgeRegistry
deactivate CIR
ISBM --> ENG : AcknowledgeRegistry
deactivate ISBM

note over ISBM, CIR
  The CIR is itself an ISBM participant.
  Registration and resolution traverse the bus —
  there is no direct registry call.
end note

ENG -> ISBM : PostPublication(SyncSegments)\non /Enterprise/Site/Eng

== 3. Governance gate ==

ISBM -> LOC : ReadPublication → SyncSegments
activate LOC
LOC -> LOC : leaf class unknown\nbind at rdl:Instrument — **degraded**
LOC -> LOC : ingest properties\nControl action arrives **mapped**

note right of LOC
  Degraded is not failed. REG-LOCATION holds the
  rdl:ControlAction *definition* but not the class
  that sanctions it. Holding a definition and holding
  the class are separate questions.
end note

LOC -> LOC : create StewardshipItem rows\ncarrying the incoming values
deactivate LOC

StewardUser -> LOC : open review queue
activate LOC
alt steward rejects
  StewardUser -> LOC : reject with reason
  LOC -> ISBM : ConfirmBOD (error)
else steward approves
  StewardUser -> LOC : approve into authoritative model
  LOC -> LOC : commit Location rows\n**carry property values forward**
  note right of LOC
    A gate that dropped the values would make
    approval lossy — the registry would publish
    less than it received.
  end note
end
deactivate LOC

LOC -> ISBM : PostRequest(ProcessRegistry)\nreuse CIRIDs from ENG entries
LOC -> ISBM : PostPublication(SyncSegments)\non /Enterprise/Site/OandM\nre-emitting mapped **and** unmapped values

== 4. Consumption ==

ISBM -> MMS : ReadPublication → SyncSegments
activate MMS
alt IdentityMap hit and still live
  MMS -> MMS : use cached CIRID
else miss, stale, or invalidated
  MMS -> ISBM : PostRequest(GetRegistry)
  activate ISBM
  ISBM -> CIR : deliver
  activate CIR
  CIR -> ISBM : ShowRegistry (CIRID cluster)
  deactivate CIR
  ISBM --> MMS : ShowRegistry
  deactivate ISBM
  MMS -> MMS : cache with StaleAfter
end

MMS -> MMS : bind or create FunctionalLocationRecord
MMS -> MMS : ingest attributes into MMS SQL\nall values retained **unmapped**

note right of MMS
  MMS holds no reference data, so it classifies
  nothing. It stores the values anyway, flagged —
  Control action included. A receiver that discarded
  what it could not classify would make federation
  all-or-nothing, and it is not.
end note
deactivate MMS

PlannerUser -> MMS : open equipment register
activate MMS
MMS --> PlannerUser : record shown with "3 identities" chip
deactivate MMS

note over PlannerUser
  No BOD is visible here. The location simply
  appeared in the maintenance system — which is
  the actual claim.
end note

== 5. Inspection ==

Demo -> UI : open /runs/{id}
activate UI

UI -> UI : **Identity** — one FederationId,\nthree codes, one minter
UI -> UI : **Results** — steps and assertions,\nconcerns separated from failures
UI -> UI : **Message flow** — every BOD,\neach row linking to its detail

Demo -> UI : open a message
UI --> Demo : source record → BOD XML →\nresulting records → provenance

Demo -> UI : Persisted data tab
UI -> ENG : read rows for the run's identities
UI -> LOC : read rows
UI -> MMS : read rows
UI --> Demo : per-participant cards\nmapped at ENG and REG-LOCATION,\nunmapped at MMS
deactivate UI

note over UI
  Read straight out of each participant's SQL schema,
  so "the data arrived" is checked rather than
  asserted. "No rows" and "store unreadable" are
  reported differently — they are different problems.
end note

@enduml
